Q: How to write unit test for switch case using jasmine A: <p>In simplest terms you don't test a switch.  </p>

<p>A switch, just like if, else, where, when and other such things are language construct, so needs no testing.  Testing a portion of your code that deals with flow control, you write different test for each outcome of the flow.</p>

<p>This means a separate suite for each option.</p>

<p><code>
    function rockPaperScisors(){
        ... 
        // switch statement for the return value
    }</p>

<pre><code>describe('rock paper scissors caller', function(){
    beforeEach(function(){
        var throw;
    });

    it("should return rock when 1 is entered", function(){
        throw = 1;
        expect(throw).toEqual('rock');
    });

    it("should return paper when 2 is entered", function(){
        throw = 2;
        expect(throw).toEqual('paper');
    });

    it("should return scissor when 3 is entered", function(){
        throw = 3;
        expect(throw).toEqual('scisor');
    });
});
</code></pre>

